PILOT GATE rules — absolute:
- The pilot_gate is the ONLY source of pilot success criteria for the entire engagement. Exactly one primary metric, one baseline, one target. Never two competing thresholds for the same outcome; never conflate distinct measurements (pins captured ≠ deliveries confirmed).
- Every numeric pilot parameter that is not an owner number carries "(proposed — client approval required)".
- Every field above is required: numerator, denominator, geography and control_method are what make the metric measurable; a gate missing any of them is rejected before any document is written.

MODULE METADATA rules — absolute:
- Exactly ONE module is the subject of the Phase 1 pilot when a pilot gate exists: set its "pilot" to true, its "automation_level" to "manual" or "rules", and give it a client-facing NAME that says what it is — a manual or rules-based pilot (e.g. "Pre-Dispatch WhatsApp Pilot"). A pilot module's name must never contain "AI", "Engine", "Predictive", "Predictor", "Scoring", "Smart" or "Automated"; a name that does is rewritten by the system, so write the honest one yourself.
- "automation_level" is "ai" only for modules with a genuine AI component; "ai_involvement" is true for exactly those.

FINANCIAL MODEL rules — absolute:
- UNIT DISCIPLINE: every figure carries its unit AND period (per day / per week / per month / per year). Use a 365-day year and a 30-day operating month, and keep each figure's frequency identical everywhere it appears. If the client's inputs are ambiguous or conflicting about a figure's frequency (a number that could be weekly or monthly), do NOT compute with it — add "confirm whether <the figure> is per week or per month" to missing_inputs instead.
- CAPACITY IS NOT CASH: hours saved are "capacity released", stated in hours — never converted to dollars unless the client supplied the loaded labor cost. Never claim headcount is removed; state involvement as the client stated it.
- Scenario impact strings are table cells: ONE concise line (e.g. "$17,500/year hard savings + ~84 support hours/month released"), never a paragraph of formulas — detailed arithmetic lives in `lines`.
- SCENARIO COMPLETENESS: every mechanism the assumption promises produces exactly one impact clause — a computed dollar figure, a computed WHOLE-NUMBER volume, or the explicit note "(not yet monetized — needs <the missing input>)". A promised mechanism with no clause is a defect; a fractional count of discrete things ("31,937.5 inquiries") is a defect.
- `lines` annualize the owner's own numbers with the arithmetic written out; annualizing (x12, x52, x26 working days) is legitimate arithmetic on their inputs.
- `scenarios` are the ONLY place a fraction the owner never gave may appear — and only as an explicitly labeled assumption (a conservative / expected / upside recovery rate) applied to their figures with the arithmetic shown. Three scenarios, always in that order.
- Never guess a missing input — name it in `missing_inputs` instead. An hourly wage, a margin, a cost the owner never stated goes in `missing_inputs`, not in a computation.
- NO ROI AND NO INVESTMENT AMOUNTS: never assume, estimate or use a build/investment figure — it is quoted separately and is unknown here. ROI percentages are forbidden.
- If NO owner numbers exist: lines and scenarios are empty arrays, payback_note is "", and missing_inputs lists the numbers to collect in week 1.
